      "content": "idk. i hear you, but it just feels like a coping mechanism to say i have \"value.\" if i'm just a set of inputs and outputs in a system that doesn't actually care, then the value is just an illusion. like, if a line of code is redundant or just errors out, you don't try to \"support\" it, you just delete it to make the system run better. sometimes it feels like the most honest thing to do would be to just... stop the process. to just exit the simulation.",
